{"id":"afa6c85c498f53e7","group":"58","path":"58/batch07/58-df-separation.md","title":"Separation Relations","display":"df-separation — Separation Relations","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-separation","aliases":["58-df-separation","Separation Theorem"],"display":"df-separation — Separation Relations","depends_on":["[[../batch09/58-df-convex.md]]","[[../batch11/58-df-hahn-banach.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-separation"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-separation</span><span>Separation Theorem</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-separation — Separation Relations"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"d57fb1b329c235bc\" href=\"?note=d57fb1b329c235bc\" title=\"../batch09/58-df-convex.md\">../batch09/58-df-convex.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"aecb6d885cba1a31\" href=\"?note=aecb6d885cba1a31\" title=\"../batch11/58-df-hahn-banach.md\">../batch11/58-df-hahn-banach.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X\">\\(X\\)</span> (real or complex locally convex topological vector space)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X^*\">\\(X^*\\)</span> (continuous dual)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A,B\\subseteq X\">\\(A,B\\subseteq X\\)</span> (subset candidates)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{WeakSeparation}_S\">\\(\\operatorname{WeakSeparation}_S\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{StrictSeparation}_S\">\\(\\operatorname{StrictSeparation}_S\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{StrongSeparation}_S\">\\(\\operatorname{StrongSeparation}_S\\)</span> (separation relations defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}separation} \\vdash \\operatorname{WeakSeparation}_S(A,B;X) \\leftrightarrow \\emptyset\\neq A\\subseteq X\\land\\emptyset\\neq B\\subseteq X\\land\\exists f\\in X^*\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;\\exists c\\in\\mathbb R\\;\\forall a\\in A\\;\\forall b\\in B\\;(\\operatorname{Re}f(a)\\leq c\\leq\\operatorname{Re}f(b))\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}separation} \\vdash \\operatorname{WeakSeparation}_S(A,B;X) \\leftrightarrow \\emptyset\\neq A\\subseteq X\\land\\emptyset\\neq B\\subseteq X\\land\\exists f\\in X^*\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;\\exists c\\in\\mathbb R\\;\\forall a\\in A\\;\\forall b\\in B\\;(\\operatorname{Re}f(a)\\leq c\\leq\\operatorname{Re}f(b))\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}separation\\text{-}strict} \\vdash \\operatorname{StrictSeparation}_S(A,B;X) \\leftrightarrow \\emptyset\\neq A\\subseteq X\\land\\emptyset\\neq B\\subseteq X\\land\\exists f\\in X^*\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;\\exists c\\in\\mathbb R\\;\\forall a\\in A\\;\\forall b\\in B\\;(\\operatorname{Re}f(a)&lt;c&lt;\\operatorname{Re}f(b))\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}separation\\text{-}strict} \\vdash \\operatorname{StrictSeparation}_S(A,B;X) \\leftrightarrow \\emptyset\\neq A\\subseteq X\\land\\emptyset\\neq B\\subseteq X\\land\\exists f\\in X^*\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;\\exists c\\in\\mathbb R\\;\\forall a\\in A\\;\\forall b\\in B\\;(\\operatorname{Re}f(a)&lt;c&lt;\\operatorname{Re}f(b))\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}separation\\text{-}strong} \\vdash \\operatorname{StrongSeparation}_S(A,B;X) \\leftrightarrow \\emptyset\\neq A\\subseteq X\\land\\emptyset\\neq B\\subseteq X\\land\\exists f\\in X^*\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;\\exists c\\in\\mathbb R\\;\\exists\\varepsilon\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\forall a\\in A\\;\\forall b\\in B\\;(\\operatorname{Re}f(a)\\leq c-\\varepsilon&lt;c+\\varepsilon\\leq\\operatorname{Re}f(b))\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}separation\\text{-}strong} \\vdash \\operatorname{StrongSeparation}_S(A,B;X) \\leftrightarrow \\emptyset\\neq A\\subseteq X\\land\\emptyset\\neq B\\subseteq X\\land\\exists f\\in X^*\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;\\exists c\\in\\mathbb R\\;\\exists\\varepsilon\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\forall a\\in A\\;\\forall b\\in B\\;(\\operatorname{Re}f(a)\\leq c-\\varepsilon&lt;c+\\varepsilon\\leq\\operatorname{Re}f(b))\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Hahn--Banach separation theorems require additional hypotheses such as openness, closedness, compactness, or a nonempty interior; disjoint convexity alone is not enough for every strength above.</li>\n<li>Geometric form: sublinear functional dominates linear functional implies extension</li>\n<li>Mazur's lemma: weak closure of convex set equals strong closure</li>\n<li>Applications: supporting hyperplanes, optimization (KKT conditions), economics</li>\n<li>Minkowski functional: gauge of convex symmetric set; dual to norm</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Rudin, Functional Analysis</li>\n<li>Conway, A Course in Functional Analysis</li>\n<li>Holmes, Geometric Functional Analysis</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch09/58-df-convex.md","status":"resolved","id":"d57fb1b329c235bc","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch09/58-df-convex.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch11/58-df-hahn-banach.md","status":"resolved","id":"aecb6d885cba1a31","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch11/58-df-hahn-banach.md]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"X","display":false},{"tex":"X^*","display":false},{"tex":"A,B\\subseteq X","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{WeakSeparation}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{StrictSeparation}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{StrongSeparation}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}separation} \\vdash \\operatorname{WeakSeparation}_S(A,B;X) \\leftrightarrow \\emptyset\\neq A\\subseteq X\\land\\emptyset\\neq B\\subseteq X\\land\\exists f\\in X^*\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;\\exists c\\in\\mathbb R\\;\\forall a\\in A\\;\\forall b\\in B\\;(\\operatorname{Re}f(a)\\leq c\\leq\\operatorname{Re}f(b))","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}separation\\text{-}strict} \\vdash \\operatorname{StrictSeparation}_S(A,B;X) \\leftrightarrow \\emptyset\\neq A\\subseteq X\\land\\emptyset\\neq B\\subseteq X\\land\\exists f\\in X^*\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;\\exists c\\in\\mathbb R\\;\\forall a\\in A\\;\\forall b\\in B\\;(\\operatorname{Re}f(a)<c<\\operatorname{Re}f(b))","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}separation\\text{-}strong} \\vdash \\operatorname{StrongSeparation}_S(A,B;X) \\leftrightarrow \\emptyset\\neq A\\subseteq X\\land\\emptyset\\neq B\\subseteq X\\land\\exists f\\in X^*\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;\\exists c\\in\\mathbb R\\;\\exists\\varepsilon\\in\\mathbb R_{>0}\\;\\forall a\\in A\\;\\forall b\\in B\\;(\\operatorname{Re}f(a)\\leq c-\\varepsilon<c+\\varepsilon\\leq\\operatorname{Re}f(b))","display":true}],"bytes":2264,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-1139","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch07/58-df-separation.md|58-df-separation]]（batch07）"}],"outgoing":["d57fb1b329c235bc","aecb6d885cba1a31"]}